      "sequence_position": 4,
      "problem": "The discrete random variable $X\\in Z$ can be approximated by the continuous random variable $Y.$ By applying an appropriate continuity correction, $P(X>-15)$ can be approximated as",
      "worked_solution": "To apply the appropriate continuity correction, we first rewrite the strict inequality as follows:\n\n$$\nP(X>-15)=P(X\\ge -14)\n$$\n\nThen, we extend the endpoint of the interval $X\\ge -14$ by $0.5:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\ge -14) & ≈P(Y\\ge -14-0.5) \\\\  & =P(Y\\ge -14.5)\\end{aligned}\n$$",
